<DocsLayout title="Fastlane Plugin" activeNav="/guides/fastlane">
  <h1>Fastlane Plugin</h1>
  <p>
    <code>fastlane-plugin-app_manager</code> connects <a href="https://fastlane.tools" target="_blank">Fastlane</a> lanes
    to the App Manager API. It provides composable actions for downloading signing credentials, managing build lifecycle,
    uploading artifacts, and inspecting app metadata &mdash; all from your <code>Fastfile</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The plugin does not own the build itself. Every download action writes to the exact <code>output_path</code> you specify,
    so the result can be combined with native Xcode/Gradle lanes, Flutter, React Native, Expo, or a custom pipeline.
  </p>

  <h2>Requirements</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Dependency</th><th>Version</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Ruby</td><td>&ge; 3.1</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Fastlane</td><td>&ge; 2.220, &lt; 3</td></tr>
      <tr><td>App Manager instance</td><td>Accessible via HTTPS (or HTTP for local dev)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Installation</h2>
  <p>The plugin is consumed as a local Bundler dependency from the monorepo. Add it to your mobile project's <code>Gemfile</code> or <code>fastlane/Pluginfile</code>:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`gem "fastlane-plugin-app_manager", path: "../libs/fastlane-plugin"`} />
  <p>Then install and verify:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`bundle install
bundle exec fastlane action app_manager_configure`} />

  <h2>Configuration</h2>
  <p>Configure the API once near the start of a lane. All subsequent actions reuse these settings:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`app_manager_configure(
  api_key: ENV.fetch("APP_MANAGER_API_KEY"),
  base_url: "https://manager.example.com",  # optional, defaults to http://localhost:8000
  team: "mobile-team",
  app: "customer-app"
)`} />

  <p>Alternatively, configure via environment variables (the configure action becomes optional):</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`export APP_MANAGER_API_KEY='1|plain-text-api-key'
export APP_MANAGER_BASE_URL='https://manager.example.com'
export APP_MANAGER_TEAM='mobile-team'
export APP_MANAGER_APP='customer-app'`} />

  <h3>Timeout and retry settings</h3>
  <p>
    The HTTP client automatically retries transient errors (HTTP 429, 502, 503, 504 and network failures)
    with exponential backoff. Customize timeouts and retry count:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`app_manager_configure(
  api_key: ENV.fetch("APP_MANAGER_API_KEY"),
  team: "mobile-team",
  app: "customer-app",
  connect_timeout: 30,   # seconds, default: 10
  read_timeout: 120,     # seconds, default: 60
  max_retries: 5         # default: 3
)`} />

  <h3>Required API scopes</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Operation</th><th>Minimum scopes</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_app_info</code></td><td><code>apps:read</code>, <code>identifiers:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_builds</code>, <code>show_build</code></td><td><code>builds:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_cancel_build</code></td><td><code>pipelines:run</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_credentials</code></td><td><code>credentials:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_identifiers</code></td><td><code>identifiers:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_artifact</code></td><td><code>artifacts:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Icon or splash-screen download</td><td><code>assets:read</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Credential download</td><td><code>credentials:read</code> (+ <code>identifiers:read</code> when <code>app_identifier</code> is omitted)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Create/start/finish a manual build</td><td><code>builds:write</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Append a build log</td><td><code>logs:write</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>Upload a build artifact</td><td><code>artifacts:write</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Actions reference</h2>
  <p>All 22 actions provided by the plugin:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Action</th><th>Description</th><th>Platforms</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Configuration &amp; metadata</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_configure</code></td><td>Configure API connection</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_app_info</code></td><td>Fetch app name, metadata and identifiers</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>

      <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Build management</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_create_build</code></td><td>Create a manual build in <code>pending</code> status</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_build_start</code></td><td>Mark build as <code>running</code></td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_build_log</code></td><td>Append plain-text log output</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_build_finish</code></td><td>Finish as <code>completed</code>, <code>failed</code>, or <code>cancelled</code></td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_builds</code></td><td>List builds with optional status filter</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_show_build</code></td><td>Show build details</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_cancel_build</code></td><td>Request build cancellation</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>

      <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Artifacts</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_add_artifact</code></td><td>Upload and attach a file to a build</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_artifact</code></td><td>Download a build artifact</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>

      <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Assets</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_icon</code></td><td>Download app icon</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_splashscreen</code></td><td>Download splash screen</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>

      <tr><td colspan="3"><strong>Credentials &amp; identifiers</strong></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_credentials</code></td><td>List all credentials for the app</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_list_identifiers</code></td><td>List app identifiers (bundle IDs, package names)</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_ios_certificate</code></td><td>Download iOS signing certificate (.p12)</td><td>iOS</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_provisioning_profile</code></td><td>Download provisioning profile</td><td>iOS</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_android_keystore</code></td><td>Download Android keystore</td><td>Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_firebase_config</code></td><td>Download Firebase service-account JSON</td><td>iOS, Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_apns_key</code></td><td>Download APNs authentication key (.p8)</td><td>iOS</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_google_play_service_account</code></td><td>Download Google Play service-account JSON</td><td>Android</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>app_manager_download_apple_api_key</code></td><td>Download App Store Connect API key (.p8)</td><td>iOS</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Shared lane context</h2>
  <p>Several actions store their result in Fastlane's lane context for use by subsequent actions:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>SharedValue</th><th>Set by</th><th>Type</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_APP_INFO</code></td><td><code>app_manager_app_info</code></td><td>App metadata hash</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_BUILD_ID</code></td><td><code>app_manager_create_build</code></td><td>Build UUID string</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_BUILDS</code></td><td><code>app_manager_list_builds</code></td><td>Array of build hashes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_BUILD_INFO</code></td><td><code>app_manager_show_build</code></td><td>Build hash</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_CREDENTIALS</code></td><td><code>app_manager_list_credentials</code></td><td>Array of credential hashes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>APP_MANAGER_IDENTIFIERS</code></td><td><code>app_manager_list_identifiers</code></td><td>Array of identifier hashes</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    Build lifecycle actions (<code>build_start</code>, <code>build_log</code>, <code>build_finish</code>,
    <code>add_artifact</code>, <code>cancel_build</code>) automatically resolve the build ID from:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>The action's explicit <code>build_id</code> parameter</li>
    <li><code>APP_MANAGER_BUILD_ID</code> in lane context (set by <code>create_build</code>)</li>
    <li>The <code>APP_MANAGER_BUILD_ID</code> environment variable (injected by CI)</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>iOS example</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`lane :ios_release do
  app_manager_configure(
    api_key: ENV.fetch("APP_MANAGER_API_KEY"),
    team: "mobile-team",
    app: "customer-app"
  )

  # Fetch app metadata
  info = app_manager_app_info
  ios_id = info[:default_app_identifiers].fetch(:ios).fetch(:identifier)

  # Download signing assets
  certificate = app_manager_download_ios_certificate(
    profile_type: "appstore",
    output_path: "build/signing/distribution.p12"
  )

  profile = app_manager_download_provisioning_profile(
    profile_type: "appstore",
    output_path: "build/signing/appstore.mobileprovision"
  )

  apple_key = app_manager_download_apple_api_key(
    output_path: "build/submission/AuthKey.p8"
  )

  # Configure signing
  import_certificate(
    certificate_path: certificate[:path],
    certificate_password: certificate[:payload]["password"]
  )

  api_key = app_store_connect_api_key(
    key_id: apple_key[:payload]["key_id"],
    issuer_id: apple_key[:payload]["issuer_id"],
    key_filepath: apple_key[:path]
  )

  install_provisioning_profile(path: profile[:path])

  # Build and upload
  build_app(
    export_options: {
      provisioningProfiles: &#123; ios_id => "Customer App Store Profile" &#125;
    }
  )
  upload_to_testflight(api_key: api_key)
end`} />

  <h2>Android example</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`lane :android_release do
  app_manager_configure(
    api_key: ENV.fetch("APP_MANAGER_API_KEY"),
    team: "mobile-team",
    app: "customer-app"
  )

  keystore = app_manager_download_android_keystore(
    profile_type: "production",
    output_path: "android/app/release.jks"
  )

  play = app_manager_download_google_play_service_account(
    output_path: "build/submission/google-play.json"
  )

  gradle(
    task: "bundle",
    build_type: "Release",
    properties: &#123;
      "android.injected.signing.store.file" => keystore[:path],
      "android.injected.signing.store.password" => keystore[:payload]["store_password"],
      "android.injected.signing.key.alias" => keystore[:payload]["key_alias"],
      "android.injected.signing.key.password" => keystore[:payload]["key_password"]
    &#125;
  )

  upload_to_play_store(json_key: play[:path])
end`} />

  <h2>Manual build lifecycle</h2>
  <p>
    Use manual reporting when App Manager cannot poll the CI provider.
    A self-hosted runner creates and owns the complete build lifecycle:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`lane :build_with_reporting do
  app_manager_configure(
    api_key: ENV.fetch("APP_MANAGER_API_KEY"),
    team: "mobile-team",
    app: "customer-app"
  )

  build = app_manager_create_build(
    profile_type: "production",
    context: &#123; commit: ENV["GITHUB_SHA"], runner: "self-hosted" &#125;
  )

  app_manager_build_start
  app_manager_build_log(message: "Resolving dependencies")

  begin
    # Your actual build steps here
    gradle(task: "bundle", build_type: "Release")

    app_manager_add_artifact(
      file: "app/build/outputs/bundle/release/app-release.aab",
      name: "app-release.aab",
      metadata: &#123; git_sha: ENV["GITHUB_SHA"] &#125;
    )

    app_manager_build_finish(status: "completed")
  rescue StandardError => error
    app_manager_build_log(message: "Build failed: #&#123;error.message&#125;")
    app_manager_build_finish(status: "failed")
    raise
  end
end`} />

  <h2>Listing and inspecting</h2>
  <p>Query builds, credentials, and identifiers from your lane:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`# List recent failed builds
builds = app_manager_list_builds(status: "failed", limit: 10)
# => [{ "id" => "...", "status" => "failed", ... }, ...]

# Show details of a specific build
build = app_manager_show_build(build_id: "build-uuid")

# Cancel a running build
app_manager_cancel_build(build_id: "build-uuid")

# List all credentials
credentials = app_manager_list_credentials
# => [{ "id" => "...", "type" => "ios_certificate", "name" => "..." }, ...]

# List all identifiers
identifiers = app_manager_list_identifiers
# => [{ "id" => "...", "platform" => "ios", "identifier" => "com.example.app" }, ...]

# Download an artifact from a previous build
app_manager_download_artifact(
  artifact_id: "artifact-uuid",
  output_path: "build/release.apk",
  build_id: "build-uuid"
)`} />

  <h2>White-label configuration</h2>
  <p>
    <code>app_manager_app_info</code> combines the configured app with its identifiers.
    The first identifier for each platform is marked as <code>default: true</code>:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`info = app_manager_app_info

info[:name]          # "Customer App"
info[:metadata]      # { "owner" => "mobile-team", "channel" => "production" }
info[:app_identifiers]
# [
#   { platform: :ios, identifier: "com.example.customer", default: true, ... },
#   { platform: :android, identifier: "com.example.customer", default: true, ... },
#   { platform: :ios, identifier: "com.example.customer.beta", default: false, ... }
# ]

# Use default identifiers directly
info[:default_app_identifiers][:ios][:identifier]
info[:default_app_identifiers][:android][:version_code]`} />
  <p>
    This makes it easy to build white-label apps: fetch the metadata once, then apply names
    and identifiers to your Xcode project or Gradle configuration.
  </p>

  <h2>CI/CD integration</h2>

  <h3>GitHub Actions</h3>
  <CodeBlock lang="yaml" code={`name: Build
on:
  workflow_dispatch:
    inputs:
      app_manager_build_id:
        required: false
        type: string

jobs:
  ios:
    runs-on: macos-latest
    env:
      APP_MANAGER_BUILD_ID: $\&#123;&#123; inputs.app_manager_build_id &#125;&#125;
      APP_MANAGER_API_KEY: $\&#123;&#123; secrets.APP_MANAGER_API_KEY &#125;&#125;
      APP_MANAGER_TEAM: mobile-team
      APP_MANAGER_APP: customer-app
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: ruby/setup-ruby@v1
        with:
          bundler-cache: true
      - run: bundle exec fastlane ios release`} />

  <h3>Bitrise</h3>
  <CodeBlock lang="yaml" code={`workflows:
  build:
    envs:
      - APP_MANAGER_API_KEY: $APP_MANAGER_API_KEY
      - APP_MANAGER_TEAM: mobile-team
      - APP_MANAGER_APP: customer-app
    steps:
      - bundle@1:
          inputs:
            - command: exec fastlane android release`} />

  <h2>Return values</h2>
  <p>Asset actions return an absolute destination path. Credential actions return a hash:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="ruby" code={`# Credential return shape
&#123;
  path: "/absolute/path/to/file",
  id: "credential-uuid",
  type: "android_keystore",
  name: "Production keystore",
  payload: &#123; "store_password" => "...", "key_alias" => "...", "key_password" => "..." &#125;,
  expires_at: "2027-07-14T00:00:00Z",
  profile_type: "production",
  app_identifier: "com.example.customer"
&#125;`} />
  <p>
    Parent directories are created automatically. Downloads use atomic writes (temp file + rename).
    Asset files use mode <code>0644</code>; credentials use mode <code>0600</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Error handling</h2>
  <p>Actions stop the lane with a Fastlane user error when configuration is missing, the API is unreachable, or a response has an unexpected shape.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>HTTP code</th><th>Likely cause</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>401</code></td><td>Missing, invalid, or revoked API key</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>403</code></td><td>Key lacks a required scope, or creator lacks team permission</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>404</code></td><td>Wrong team/app slug, cross-team resource, or missing file</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>409</code></td><td>Build is automatic or has a conflicting terminal state</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>422</code></td><td>Invalid build profile, payload, or artifact metadata</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The plugin automatically retries on transient errors (429, 502, 503, 504) and network failures
    with exponential backoff. Use <code>app_manager_configure</code> to adjust <code>max_retries</code>.
  </p>
  <p>Common non-HTTP errors:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Fix</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>Multiple App Manager credentials match</code></td><td>Add <code>credential_id</code> or a unique <code>credential_name</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td>No platform identifier</td><td>Create an identifier in App Manager or pass <code>app_identifier</code> explicitly</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>Refusing to overwrite</code></td><td>Set <code>overwrite: true</code> or choose a fresh destination</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`# Inspect available options for any action
bundle exec fastlane action app_manager_download_android_keystore

# Check plugin installation
bundle exec fastlane action app_manager_configure

# Run tests locally
cd libs/fastlane-plugin
bundle install
bundle exec rspec`} />
</DocsLayout>
